+### 4.3 list_sessions
+
+Requests a page of the authenticated user's conversation summaries. The frame carries no trusted identity: the server uses the user authenticated at the WebSocket upgrade and ignores an extra `userId` field ([validated by: answers list_sessions for the authenticated user with ISO dates, forwarding limit and before while ignoring any client userId](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L97)).
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "list_sessions",
+  "limit": 10,
+  "before": {"sessionId": "previous-session", "updatedAt": "2026-01-15T14:30:00.000Z"}
+}
+```
+
+| Field              | Type           | Required  | Description                                     |
+| ------------------ | -------------- | --------- | ----------------------------------------------- |
+| `type`             | string         | Yes       | `"list_sessions"`                               |
+| `limit`            | integer        | No        | Non-negative page size                          |
+| `before`           | object         | No        | Cursor after the last summary on the prior page |
+| `before.sessionId` | string         | If before | Session id, 1–128 Unicode characters            |
+| `before.updatedAt` | string, number | If before | Timestamp parseable as a date                   |
+
+An invalid paging field receives `INVALID_MESSAGE` without querying the store ([validated by: accepts a bare list_sessions frame and rejects a malformed limit or before with INVALID_MESSAGE without calling listFor](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L167), [validated by: counts Unicode characters in a list_sessions cursor id](../../src/transport/ws/sessionCursorUnicode.test.ts#L4)).
 
