+### 5.9 session_list
+
+Answers a `list_sessions` request with conversation metadata for the connection's authenticated user, never conversation content. Each summary contains only its session id, creation and last activity times as ISO-8601 strings, and entry count ([validated by: answers list_sessions for the authenticated user with ISO dates, forwarding limit and before while ignoring any client userId](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L97)).
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "session_list",
+  "sessions": [
+    {
+      "sessionId": "previous-session",
+      "createdAt": "2026-01-14T12:00:00.000Z",
+      "updatedAt": "2026-01-15T14:30:00.000Z",
+      "entryCount": 2
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+| Field                   | Type     | Description                               |
+| ----------------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------- |
+| `type`                  | string   | `"session_list"`                          |
+| `sessions`              | object[] | Summaries, newest activity first          |
+| `sessions[].sessionId`  | string   | Id used to reconnect to this conversation |
+| `sessions[].createdAt`  | string   | ISO-8601 creation time                    |
+| `sessions[].updatedAt`  | string   | ISO-8601 last activity time               |
+| `sessions[].entryCount` | number   | Number of conversation entries            |
+
+A client opens a listed conversation by reconnecting with its `sessionId` in the query string as described in §2.1. If the store has no `listFor`, the server answers an empty `session_list`; if listing throws, it sends `SERVER_ERROR` and keeps the socket open ([validated by: answers an empty session_list when the store has no listFor, and SERVER_ERROR with a ws error log when listFor throws](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L138)).
+
